**How to implement.** `buildDesign` hands each kept row's label reading to its per-row projection, so no projection reads a label again and the staged path (step 351) is total without an arm for an `Error` that cannot occur (AGENTS.md 'Errors are values'; the S10.3 brief 'The test-only failure helpers … become typed errors'). Since step 270, `buildDesign` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:buildDesign`) keeps a row only when `NamingTemplate.standard.readName r.experiment.nameText` reads it, and the section 7.2 fact's `prepareRow` reads the same label again and fails the fact on an `Error` that no kept row can give. (1) In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`, `buildDesign`'s first parameter becomes `prepareRow : MuellerRawRow -> NameReading -> StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity`. Each row's label is read once. A row is kept, in row order and with its reading, when the reading's `matrixKind` equals `kind`, the label is no AIR#0 label and the row is no excluded point, as today; each kept row is projected by `prepareRow row reading`. The rows kept, their order and the system are unchanged. Its doc says so in one to three lines (spec 0050 S10.3). No other declaration changes. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact's `prepareRow` takes `(reading : NameReading)` after its row and its φ is `reading.objectPhi`; its own read of the label and the failure on that read's `Error` (step 270) are deleted. `buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)`'s stub projection takes an ignored `NameReading` after its row; its rows, its assertions and its numbers are unchanged. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the reading `buildDesign` hands over is the reading the fact made itself, so every row has the same φ and every design row the same entries. No test is added or removed. No other consumer of `buildDesign` exists: the S10.3 path adopts this form in step 351.

**Acceptance.** After the change, `buildDesign`'s projection MUST have the type `MuellerRawRow -> NameReading -> StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity` and receive each kept row's reading, and no projection in `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST read a label; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.
